{#
  The general-purpose platform notification, as an ordered parameter list.

  ONE PARAMETER PER LINE, in order. Blank lines are dropped by
  `services/whatsapp_templates.py`, so control flow can be indented freely without
  producing an empty slot.

  Rendered by the NON-escaping Jinja environment, which is the safe setting here:
  a parameter is delivered as text into a slot in an approved template and is
  never markup, so escaping would put `&#39;` into a French case description on
  somebody's phone. Whitespace inside a parameter is collapsed by
  `core.whatsapp.sanitize_parameter`, because the Cloud API refuses a body
  parameter containing a newline, a tab, or four consecutive spaces.

  Every value here comes from `chrome` or from the notification itself. There is
  deliberately no wording of its own and no `{% if language %}` branch — the
  localization lives in `core/notifications.py` and `core/whatsapp.py` beside the
  rest of the platform's text, so this file is structure and nothing else.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE APPROVED TEMPLATE THIS MATCHES
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Register a template named `notification`, category UTILITY, in each language
  the deployment sends (fr, ar, en_US), with a body of exactly four variables:

      {{1}}

      *{{2}}*
      {{3}}

      {{4}}

  {{1}} greeting        — "Bonjour Amina"
  {{2}} title           — the notification's heading, from core/notifications.py
  {{3}} message         — the notification's sentence, same source
  {{4}} where to read it — the deep link, or a sentence saying to open the
                           platform when no base URL is configured

  The count and the order below ARE the contract with that template. Changing
  either without re-submitting the template produces error 132000 on every
  message — which is recorded as `template_rejected`, one delivery at a time.
#}
{{ chrome.greeting }}
{{ title }}
{{ message }}
{% if action_url %}
{{ chrome.action_label }}: {{ action_url }}
{% else %}
{{ chrome.no_link }}
{% endif %}
